517
00:19:13,291 --> 00:19:16,360
(The final boss who could finally win him over has appeared.)

518
00:19:16,361 --> 00:19:18,260
- Let's do it today.
- I wish I did.

519
00:19:18,261 --> 00:19:19,430
Let's do it today.

520
00:19:19,431 --> 00:19:20,431
(It seems My Star claimed the top spot.)

521
00:19:20,432 --> 00:19:22,630
You have something in common.

522
00:19:22,631 --> 00:19:24,501
You both have dimples in pretty much the same spot.

523
00:19:25,101 --> 00:19:27,470
- You have 1 here. I have 2 here.
- The thing...

524
00:19:27,471 --> 00:19:29,870
with people with dimples is...

525
00:19:29,871 --> 00:19:31,040
What now?

526
00:19:31,041 --> 00:19:33,970
You can't get anything too intense when you have skin treatments.

527
00:19:33,971 --> 00:19:35,540
Or your dimples disappear.

528
00:19:35,541 --> 00:19:36,940
That's why I can't do anything here.

529
00:19:36,941 --> 00:19:38,710
- You can't.
- Is that so?

530
00:19:38,711 --> 00:19:40,881
That's why you didn't lose much fat from your face...

531
00:19:41,981 --> 00:19:43,350
- even after the treatment.
- Yes.

532
00:19:43,351 --> 00:19:46,921
- You're right.
- That's why it's still chubby.

533
00:19:47,321 --> 00:19:48,820
(Glaring)

534
00:19:48,821 --> 00:19:51,820
- What I mean is, you look healthy.
- You're so annoying.

535
00:19:51,821 --> 00:19:53,160
You look healthy.

536
00:19:53,161 --> 00:19:54,331
(The 2nd-in-command secretary gets on her nerves.)

537
00:19:54,631 --> 00:19:56,901
I have no energy because I haven't eaten anything.

538
00:19:57,501 --> 00:19:59,571
Your face is chubby, which is nice.

539
00:19:59,901 --> 00:20:01,131
What do you mean, my face is chubby?

540
00:20:01,271 --> 00:20:04,200
- Your face...
- You're getting on my nerves.

541
00:20:04,201 --> 00:20:05,270
- Your face...
- I mean...

542
00:20:05,271 --> 00:20:07,810
You lost a lot of weight, but your face...

543
00:20:07,811 --> 00:20:10,010
My face just doesn't seem to lose fat.

544
00:20:10,011 --> 00:20:13,181
I told you. Your face is still chubby.

545
00:20:13,981 --> 00:20:15,580
- My face...
- Your face is chubby.

546
00:20:15,581 --> 00:20:17,881
- Only your arms are slim.
- You're so annoying.

547
00:20:18,121 --> 00:20:19,450
That doesn't look normal.

548
00:20:19,451 --> 00:20:20,520
Only your arms are slim.

549
00:20:20,521 --> 00:20:23,620
You look like E.T.

550
00:20:23,621 --> 00:20:25,260
Are you kidding me?

551
00:20:25,261 --> 00:20:26,430
(Exploding)

552
00:20:26,431 --> 00:20:28,131
What are you talking about?

553
00:20:29,161 --> 00:20:30,431
Do I look that bad?

554
00:20:31,431 --> 00:20:33,031
- Only your arms are slim.
- Do I look that bad?

555
00:20:33,901 --> 00:20:36,170
No. Your face looks perfectly healthy.

556
00:20:36,171 --> 00:20:37,670
It's just that your arms look too slim.

557
00:20:37,671 --> 00:20:39,040
- Come on.
- Compared to your arms...

558
00:20:39,041 --> 00:20:40,140
- Hey.
- What?

559
00:20:40,141 --> 00:20:41,370
Tell her that she looks pretty.

560
00:20:41,371 --> 00:20:42,940
What I'm saying is, she looks healthy and good.

561
00:20:42,941 --> 00:20:44,011
Seo Jin!

562
00:20:44,411 --> 00:20:46,010
- I mean...
- Mr. Secretary!

563
00:20:46,011 --> 00:20:47,081
(Startled)

564
00:20:47,251 --> 00:20:49,380
(Seo Jin!)

565
00:20:49,381 --> 00:20:50,821
(Mr. Secretary!)

566
00:20:50,881 --> 00:20:54,351
I mean, I like that you look healthy.

567
00:20:54,851 --> 00:20:56,790
You can edit the photos anyway.

568
00:20:56,791 --> 00:20:58,090
To make your face look slimmer.

569
00:20:58,091 --> 00:20:59,291
Only your arms look slim, though.

570
00:21:00,891 --> 00:21:02,531
So you're saying I look weird!

571
00:21:02,801 --> 00:21:05,101
You look healthy.

572
00:21:05,361 --> 00:21:06,900
You look healthy and great.

573
00:21:06,901 --> 00:21:07,901
(Shivering)

574
00:21:08,501 --> 00:21:11,001
(Shaking his head)

575
00:21:11,271 --> 00:21:14,670
Her voice is way too high-pitched.

576
00:21:14,671 --> 00:21:16,081
She sounds like...

577
00:21:16,511 --> 00:21:19,051
she's freaking out.

578
00:21:20,711 --> 00:21:21,811
Mr. Secretary!

579
00:21:22,851 --> 00:21:23,950
(It's so fun to tease her.)

580
00:21:23,951 --> 00:21:26,650
I didn't know your voice was this high.

581
00:21:26,651 --> 00:21:28,861
(Her voice is too loud for someone who is turning over a new leaf.)

582
00:21:28,991 --> 00:21:30,960
You always had a high singing voice.

583
00:21:30,961 --> 00:21:33,061
- Yes. I sing in a high register.
- You sing in a high register.

584
00:21:34,261 --> 00:21:35,261
- That'd make you a good singer.
- Yes.

585
00:21:35,262 --> 00:21:36,301
She's great.

586
00:21:36,861 --> 00:21:38,261
She's rather underestimated.

587
00:21:39,201 --> 00:21:40,871
- I'm quite good.
- Usually...

588
00:21:41,431 --> 00:21:43,571
She was known more for dancing than singing,

589
00:21:44,241 --> 00:21:45,840
so her vocal talent was often overlooked.

590
00:21:45,841 --> 00:21:48,141
Right. You won "Immortal Songs" too.

591
00:21:49,581 --> 00:21:50,710
(These two are no pushovers.)

592
00:21:50,711 --> 00:21:51,981
I brought him.

593
00:21:52,511 --> 00:21:54,450
- Well...
- Have you eaten?

594
00:21:54,451 --> 00:21:57,020
- No, I haven't. What's this?
- You haven't?

595
00:21:57,021 --> 00:21:58,320
"In Young Mushroom?" What's this?

596
00:21:58,321 --> 00:21:59,450
- Is there a snack like this?
- My fan...

597
00:21:59,451 --> 00:22:01,350
- No. My fan made it.
- Your fan made it?

598
00:22:01,351 --> 00:22:02,360
(Her fan made the snack for her.)

599
00:22:02,361 --> 00:22:03,520
I have an amazing fan like that.

600
00:22:03,521 --> 00:22:06,891
I thought it was an actual snack.

601
00:22:08,091 --> 00:22:09,560
I heard you were really popular these days,

602
00:22:09,561 --> 00:22:11,160
but was it this much?

603
00:22:11,161 --> 00:22:12,270
(I heard you're really popular these days, but was it this much?)

604
00:22:12,271 --> 00:22:14,330
Seo Jin, I used to be popular...

605
00:22:14,331 --> 00:22:15,940
when you saw me back in the day.

606
00:22:15,941 --> 00:22:17,340
- You were more popular then.
- Right.

607
00:22:17,341 --> 00:22:18,670
You were popular then,

608
00:22:18,671 --> 00:22:20,010
but your popularity went down.

609
00:22:20,011 --> 00:22:21,470
(But it went down.)

610
00:22:21,471 --> 00:22:22,710
Your popularity went down.

611
00:22:22,711 --> 00:22:23,980
That's right. I took a long break.

612
00:22:23,981 --> 00:22:26,150
- That's right. With all the issues.
- Yes.

613
00:22:26,151 --> 00:22:28,150
- But now...
- You're back up now.

614
00:22:28,151 --> 00:22:29,450
Yes. I'm back.

615
00:22:29,451 --> 00:22:31,981
(Having her in the palm of his hand)

616
00:22:32,221 --> 00:22:36,091
It's the era where people like Seo In Young are back in style.

617
00:22:36,521 --> 00:22:37,821
(Listen to him talk.)

618
00:22:38,121 --> 00:22:44,331
Let's check your qualities as a manager here.

619
00:22:44,461 --> 00:22:48,331
Why do you think my style works now?

620
00:22:49,101 --> 00:22:52,541
(My Star asked a difficult question.)

621
00:22:56,311 --> 00:22:58,080
You should go first.

622
00:22:58,081 --> 00:22:59,650
- Why?
- I...

623
00:22:59,651 --> 00:23:00,750
I haven't even watched them.

624
00:23:00,751 --> 00:23:02,220
- You watched her videos.
- I mean...

625
00:23:02,221 --> 00:23:03,550
you'd know...

626
00:23:03,551 --> 00:23:06,021
- that I'm popular these days.
- That's right.

627
00:23:06,091 --> 00:23:07,720
Why do you think I'm popular?

628
00:23:07,721 --> 00:23:08,861
Why?

629
00:23:09,091 --> 00:23:10,190
- I'm sorry.
- What is that?

630
00:23:10,191 --> 00:23:11,961
What is that sound? You're working.

631
00:23:12,431 --> 00:23:13,560
- I'm...
- You're working.

632
00:23:13,561 --> 00:23:15,530
- Come on!
- I just...

633
00:23:15,531 --> 00:23:18,361
There's always someone like that even in church.

634
00:23:18,931 --> 00:23:21,830
- Put it on vibrate. You're working.
- On vibrate.

635
00:23:21,831 --> 00:23:23,201
That's your charm.

636
00:23:23,401 --> 00:23:26,371
- You're working.
- That's your charm.

637
00:23:27,211 --> 00:23:29,711
(What is he talking about?)

638
00:23:29,811 --> 00:23:32,380
Someone who doesn't look like she would go to church...

639
00:23:32,381 --> 00:23:33,411
goes to church.

640
00:23:34,351 --> 00:23:37,320
- Right? I think that's a charm.
- I...

641
00:23:37,321 --> 00:23:39,250
saw her wear the choir robe...

642
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:41,150
- Right.
- and sing.

643
00:23:41,151 --> 00:23:43,161
That was so funny.

644
00:23:43,221 --> 00:23:45,520
It really didn't suit her.

645
00:23:45,521 --> 00:23:46,730
She looks like...

646
00:23:46,731 --> 00:23:49,501
she'd spit on people at church.

647
00:23:50,801 --> 00:23:53,000
But she was there singing.

648
00:23:53,001 --> 00:23:55,770
That's a contrasting charm.

649
00:23:55,771 --> 00:23:56,900
- That's funny.
- That's the charm.

650
00:23:56,901 --> 00:23:58,040
That's funny.

651
00:23:58,041 --> 00:23:59,740
- A contrasting charm?
- Yes.

652
00:23:59,741 --> 00:24:01,441
- You have that.
- What else?

653
00:24:01,841 --> 00:24:03,210
That's the first one.

654
00:24:03,211 --> 00:24:05,950
This is how the redemption story works.

655
00:24:05,951 --> 00:24:07,081
I honestly...

656
00:24:07,111 --> 00:24:09,681
used to swear a lot.

657
00:24:09,781 --> 00:24:11,980
But I'll atone for it now...

658
00:24:11,981 --> 00:24:13,121
- Yes.
- while going to church.

659
00:24:13,191 --> 00:24:14,250
I'll pray...

660
00:24:14,251 --> 00:24:15,390
and become a new person.

661
00:24:15,391 --> 00:24:17,020
That's what people like.

662
00:24:17,021 --> 00:24:19,090
It's an era of forgiving.

663
00:24:19,091 --> 00:24:21,631
Those who haven't forgiven me still haven't forgiven me.

664
00:24:21,691 --> 00:24:24,831
You can't expect everyone to do so.

665
00:24:25,531 --> 00:24:27,700
- More than half is enough.
- Right.

666
00:24:27,701 --> 00:24:29,871
That would be enough.

667
00:24:29,941 --> 00:24:31,940
- That's what you think.
- Yes. That's what I think.

668
00:24:31,941 --> 00:24:33,071
Fifty percent.

669
00:24:33,241 --> 00:24:35,640
(The secretary who controls My Star's mood)

670
00:24:35,641 --> 00:24:38,481
There's something I prepared for you.

671
00:24:40,181 --> 00:24:41,650
First of all,

672
00:24:41,651 --> 00:24:43,250
you have to listen.

673
00:24:43,251 --> 00:24:46,421
I think managers are characters...

674
00:24:46,621 --> 00:24:48,851
who represent me wherever they go.

675
00:24:49,321 --> 00:24:51,761
So I don't like anything that's tacky.

676
00:24:52,021 --> 00:24:55,630
You have to dress according to the time and occasion.

677
00:24:55,631 --> 00:24:57,600
I'd like you...

678
00:24:57,601 --> 00:24:59,171
to get changed into clothes that are my style.

679
00:24:59,271 --> 00:25:01,501
- I prepared these gifts.
- Really?

680
00:25:01,531 --> 00:25:02,701
Yes.

681
00:25:03,101 --> 00:25:06,210
(The uniforms My Star actually prepared)

682
00:25:06,211 --> 00:25:09,010
(Wig, hoodie, pants)

683
00:25:09,011 --> 00:25:10,040
(My Star's favourite hip-hop style)

684
00:25:10,041 --> 00:25:11,410
Look. Hip-hop.

685
00:25:11,411 --> 00:25:12,880
- Look. Hip-hop.
- This...

686
00:25:12,881 --> 00:25:14,711
- Isn't this worse?
- No. Yours is worse.

687
00:25:14,851 --> 00:25:16,220
Do you know what this is?

688
00:25:16,221 --> 00:25:18,780
This is an outfit you wear...

689
00:25:18,781 --> 00:25:20,420
when you're meeting someone for the third time on a blind date.

690
00:25:20,421 --> 00:25:22,290
- Really?
- Yes.

691
00:25:22,291 --> 00:25:23,560
- What about this?
- This...

692
00:25:23,561 --> 00:25:24,590
- This...
- What's with the wig?

693
00:25:24,591 --> 00:25:25,620
- We have to wear wigs?
- Today...

694
00:25:25,621 --> 00:25:26,761
Of course.

695
00:25:27,091 --> 00:25:29,260
Try it on and then talk.

696
00:25:29,261 --> 00:25:30,561
That's your hairstyle.

697
00:25:31,601 --> 00:25:33,630
Why are you using your hairstyle?

698
00:25:33,631 --> 00:25:35,740
- Seo Jin.
- You want us to look the same.

699
00:25:35,741 --> 00:25:38,740
- You came to represent me today.
- Yes.

700
00:25:38,741 --> 00:25:41,041
- You'll do it anyway...
- Did you hurt your finger?

701
00:25:41,111 --> 00:25:42,141
Yesterday...

702
00:25:42,511 --> 00:25:45,181
(An unexpected sweet concern)

703
00:25:45,481 --> 00:25:48,080
(He's worried about My Star's hand before the photo shoot.)

704
00:25:48,081 --> 00:25:50,551
Yesterday, I cut it while cutting some peaches.

705
00:25:50,751 --> 00:25:53,121
You said you were on a diet. You're taking lots of sugar.

706
00:25:55,451 --> 00:25:56,790
I also...

707
00:25:56,791 --> 00:25:58,861
I also ate jjamppong and all.

708
00:25:59,131 --> 00:26:00,460
- All right.
- There's a changing room there.

709
00:26:00,461 --> 00:26:01,861
- Where?
- Here.

710
00:26:02,261 --> 00:26:03,901
It's going to be hot in these.

711
00:26:05,001 --> 00:26:06,330
It's so hot.

712
00:26:06,331 --> 00:26:08,471
(Genie will wear anything for My Star.)

713
00:26:11,241 --> 00:26:12,770
Ta-da!

714
00:26:12,771 --> 00:26:13,811
It's hot.

715
00:26:14,771 --> 00:26:16,110
(A hip-hop duo in their 50s)

716
00:26:16,111 --> 00:26:17,311
You look so cool!

717
00:26:17,981 --> 00:26:19,680
It's nice but hot.

718
00:26:19,681 --> 00:26:20,811
It's for summer.

719
00:26:21,211 --> 00:26:23,050
- It's for summer.
- But it's so thick.

720
00:26:23,051 --> 00:26:24,220
You have to close that.

721
00:26:24,221 --> 00:26:26,290
Don't keep it open. You look like an old man.

722
00:26:26,291 --> 00:26:27,951
You look so nice.

723
00:26:28,351 --> 00:26:30,521
You look so nice.

724
00:26:30,861 --> 00:26:32,991
It's hot. It's fine, but...

725
00:26:33,131 --> 00:26:35,691
You should endure that for the fashion.

726
00:26:35,801 --> 00:26:37,001
Come here.

727
00:26:37,361 --> 00:26:39,871
(It's time to wear the bowl cut wig.)

728
00:26:40,601 --> 00:26:42,030
Your head...

729
00:26:42,031 --> 00:26:43,870
(He willingly lowers his head.)

730
00:26:43,871 --> 00:26:46,241
- Is this how you wear it?
- Yes. You wear it like this.

731
00:26:47,671 --> 00:26:48,671
(Exclaiming)

732
00:26:48,841 --> 00:26:50,681
- Do we look like siblings?
- It's really... Yes.

733
00:26:51,141 --> 00:26:52,951
We look like siblings. Look.

734
00:26:53,481 --> 00:26:54,551
Look.

735
00:26:54,611 --> 00:26:56,380
He looks good. What's happening?

736
00:26:56,381 --> 00:26:57,521
(The sibling with dimples from the US)

737
00:26:57,951 --> 00:27:00,151
(He's not so sure.)

738
00:27:00,421 --> 00:27:02,251
Is it because it's your hairstyle?

739
00:27:02,561 --> 00:27:04,361
It looks cool. Come here.

740
00:27:04,821 --> 00:27:05,860
Kwang Kyu.

741
00:27:05,861 --> 00:27:07,261
(It's Kwang Kyu's turn.)

742
00:27:07,861 --> 00:27:10,601
I can't wear wigs because my head gets hot.

743
00:27:10,831 --> 00:27:12,061
No.

744
00:27:12,871 --> 00:27:14,070
No...

745
00:27:14,071 --> 00:27:15,871
- I get sweaty easily.
- Let me just see.

746
00:27:16,601 --> 00:27:17,841
Look.

747
00:27:18,641 --> 00:27:20,710
This is hip-hop!

748
00:27:20,711 --> 00:27:23,440
(The big sister, Hip Kwang Kyu)

749
00:27:23,441 --> 00:27:26,311
This is like Seo In Young and Boys.

750
00:27:26,781 --> 00:27:27,981
Look!

751
00:27:28,511 --> 00:27:30,481
This is amazing.

752
00:27:32,891 --> 00:27:35,520
(Happy)

753
00:27:35,521 --> 00:27:37,060
This is what it looks like.

754
00:27:37,061 --> 00:27:38,420
(He doesn't really hate having hair after a while.)

755
00:27:38,421 --> 00:27:39,761
I'll lower the temperature setting.

756
00:27:40,491 --> 00:27:42,800
You look good. I was trying to make things funny,

757
00:27:42,801 --> 00:27:45,631
but why do they look good?

758
00:27:46,931 --> 00:27:49,001
We'll wear them later. It's so hot right now.

759
00:27:50,001 --> 00:27:52,241
- I should pull my pants up a bit.
- No, keep them down.

760
00:27:52,641 --> 00:27:53,710
No.

761
00:27:53,711 --> 00:27:54,811
Don't pull them up.

762
00:27:55,311 --> 00:27:56,880
You should keep it sagging like hip-hop.

763
00:27:56,881 --> 00:27:58,980
These days, you just wear them low on your hips.

764
00:27:58,981 --> 00:28:00,480
- But they'll get dragged.
- Right.

765
00:28:00,481 --> 00:28:01,710
That's right.

766
00:28:01,711 --> 00:28:02,821
Right.

767
00:28:02,951 --> 00:28:04,050
My mom will scold me.

768
00:28:04,051 --> 00:28:05,580
No. Keep them like that.

769
00:28:05,581 --> 00:28:06,851
- Okay.
- Okay.

770
00:28:07,321 --> 00:28:10,291
I should do as the princess says.

771
00:28:10,421 --> 00:28:11,690
- Princess.
- Princess.

772
00:28:11,691 --> 00:28:13,590
Princess!

773
00:28:13,591 --> 00:28:15,230
(The magic word that makes her happy, "Princess")

774
00:28:15,231 --> 00:28:17,000
She likes it.

775
00:28:17,001 --> 00:28:18,731
Princess. Gosh.

776
00:28:20,471 --> 00:28:21,671
I heard...

777
00:28:22,071 --> 00:28:23,870
you were not on a diet for today's shoot.

778
00:28:23,871 --> 00:28:26,540
- It's for the Waterbomb Festival.
