00:59:14,791 --> 00:59:15,991
I...

1573
00:59:17,251 --> 00:59:19,660
Don't lower your chin too much.

1574
00:59:19,661 --> 00:59:20,890
No? Okay.

1575
00:59:20,891 --> 00:59:22,631
- Keep your chin up.
- Up?

1576
00:59:22,691 --> 00:59:24,731
And don't look too forward.

1577
00:59:24,861 --> 00:59:26,561
- Okay.
- Tilt your head.

1578
00:59:26,701 --> 00:59:28,171
- Sideways?
- Like this.

1579
00:59:28,231 --> 00:59:29,400
- Okay.
- Glare at the camera.

1580
00:59:29,401 --> 00:59:30,401
- You know what to do.
- Okay.

1581
00:59:30,402 --> 00:59:33,171
Why do you keep your chin down?

1582
00:59:33,601 --> 00:59:36,010
- That's not good.
- Okay.

1583
00:59:36,011 --> 00:59:37,471
(The thinker secretary also knows how to compliment.)

1584
00:59:37,541 --> 00:59:39,680
You're good at photo shoots.

1585
00:59:39,681 --> 00:59:40,840
(Sweet life hack from the photo shoot master)

1586
00:59:40,841 --> 00:59:43,680
I don't look good in front.

1587
00:59:43,681 --> 00:59:45,281
So I always tilt my head.

1588
00:59:45,721 --> 00:59:48,521
If I keep my chin down, you can't really see it.

1589
00:59:48,651 --> 00:59:51,091
But when looking sideways, you need to tilt your head.

1590
00:59:51,621 --> 00:59:53,520
If you tilt your head,

1591
00:59:53,521 --> 00:59:55,030
you can see this side.

1592
00:59:55,031 --> 00:59:56,091
(Try Seo Genie's advice.)

1593
00:59:56,531 --> 00:59:59,930
(Waiting for My Star to get changed)

1594
00:59:59,931 --> 01:00:01,471
I have a runny nose.

1595
01:00:03,201 --> 01:00:04,331
Tissue, please.

1596
01:00:04,701 --> 01:00:06,500
(My Star has a runny nose.)

1597
01:00:06,501 --> 01:00:07,701
Thank you.

1598
01:00:08,511 --> 01:00:11,910
(Wiping her nose with the tissue)

1599
01:00:11,911 --> 01:00:13,180
Watch your nails.

1600
01:00:13,181 --> 01:00:14,240
(Detailed)

1601
01:00:14,241 --> 01:00:15,711
It'll go in your nose.

1602
01:00:15,811 --> 01:00:16,980
Here you are.

1603
01:00:16,981 --> 01:00:19,621
(Taking care of the dirty tissue)

1604
01:00:21,151 --> 01:00:22,221
(Groaning)

1605
01:00:24,121 --> 01:00:26,820
(My Star is starting to get tired.)

1606
01:00:26,821 --> 01:00:28,430
Let me check your nose.

1607
01:00:28,431 --> 01:00:29,760
(Worried)

1608
01:00:29,761 --> 01:00:30,891
I'm leaving.

1609
01:00:30,931 --> 01:00:32,130
Let me fix your lips.

1610
01:00:32,131 --> 01:00:33,601
No.

1611
01:00:33,901 --> 01:00:35,001
Give me that.

1612
01:00:36,301 --> 01:00:37,601
I don't want to fix my lips.

1613
01:00:37,771 --> 01:00:39,140
Come on. Fix it.

1614
01:00:39,141 --> 01:00:40,470
No.

1615
01:00:40,471 --> 01:00:42,011
- Fix it.
- No.

1616
01:00:42,071 --> 01:00:43,370
I don't want to.

1617
01:00:43,371 --> 01:00:44,440
I have to get changed too.

1618
01:00:44,441 --> 01:00:46,240
- She doesn't like it?
- In Young hates...

1619
01:00:46,241 --> 01:00:47,381
applying lip gloss.

1620
01:00:47,611 --> 01:00:49,350
She always refuses to put it on.

1621
01:00:49,351 --> 01:00:50,480
Then don't do it.

1622
01:00:50,481 --> 01:00:51,520
She has to.

1623
01:00:51,521 --> 01:00:53,121
For the photo shoot.

1624
01:00:53,321 --> 01:00:55,791
Her lips need to look moist.

1625
01:00:56,491 --> 01:00:57,691
No.

1626
01:00:57,751 --> 01:00:58,990
- Sit down.
- No.

1627
01:00:58,991 --> 01:01:00,120
Then you do it for me.

1628
01:01:00,121 --> 01:01:02,261
- I can't do that.
- You're my secretary.

1629
01:01:02,831 --> 01:01:05,960
(Treat her like a 5-year-old boy.)

1630
01:01:05,961 --> 01:01:07,300
Do it for me.

1631
01:01:07,301 --> 01:01:08,971
- Put the lip gloss on me.
- You want me to do it?

1632
01:01:09,371 --> 01:01:10,671
The other way.

1633
01:01:12,171 --> 01:01:13,600
The other way.

1634
01:01:13,601 --> 01:01:14,711
(Genie will even babysit.)

1635
01:01:17,981 --> 01:01:21,011
(Yet he's careful.)

1636
01:01:21,081 --> 01:01:22,280
I think you're erasing it.

1637
01:01:22,281 --> 01:01:24,780
(Kwang Kyu watches them closely.)

1638
01:01:24,781 --> 01:01:25,781
(Wait a minute.)

1639
01:01:25,782 --> 01:01:26,951
We're not ready for the shoot yet.

1640
01:01:27,991 --> 01:01:30,690
They seem to have a lot in common...

1641
01:01:30,691 --> 01:01:31,860
for being mean.

1642
01:01:31,861 --> 01:01:34,220
(For being mean)

1643
01:01:34,221 --> 01:01:35,890
They keep muttering.

1644
01:01:35,891 --> 01:01:37,291
They go, "I'm not doing it. I don't want to do it."

1645
01:01:38,661 --> 01:01:41,600
(My Star hates applying anything on her lips.)

1646
01:01:41,601 --> 01:01:43,731
(And neither does Seo Jin.)

1647
01:01:44,231 --> 01:01:47,640
(My Star hates waiting.)

1648
01:01:47,641 --> 01:01:51,741
(Seo Jin doesn't know what it means to wait.)

1649
01:01:53,711 --> 01:01:55,711
They both have...

1650
01:01:56,011 --> 01:01:57,281
the same dimples.

1651
01:01:57,351 --> 01:01:58,650
As if they were siblings,

1652
01:01:58,651 --> 01:02:01,121
they both have dimples.

1653
01:02:02,021 --> 01:02:04,190
I think they have a lot in common.

1654
01:02:04,191 --> 01:02:05,421
(They have the same dimples as if they were siblings.)

1655
01:02:06,061 --> 01:02:07,890
Let's get to it!

1656
01:02:07,891 --> 01:02:08,891
- Okay.
- Are you ready?

1657
01:02:08,892 --> 01:02:09,931
Let's do this.

1658
01:02:10,091 --> 01:02:12,261
Here comes the princess!

1659
01:02:12,601 --> 01:02:14,801
Here comes the princess!

1660
01:02:15,331 --> 01:02:16,800
- Hi.
- Hi.

1661
01:02:16,801 --> 01:02:18,141
(The princess is happy about the shout-out.)

1662
01:02:18,901 --> 01:02:21,310
Our dear princess. How pretty.

1663
01:02:21,311 --> 01:02:23,971
(5-year-old mode off, work mode on)

1664
01:02:25,511 --> 01:02:27,241
Can you look down a little?

1665
01:02:27,441 --> 01:02:28,481
That's it.

1666
01:02:28,881 --> 01:02:31,321
(Moving straight to the next outfit)

1667
01:02:32,421 --> 01:02:37,821
(The shoot continues for 3 hours without a break.)

1668
01:02:38,261 --> 01:02:39,291
Nice.

1669
01:02:41,691 --> 01:02:44,391
(My Star is quickly wearing out.)

1670
01:02:45,061 --> 01:02:46,100
She's cool.

1671
01:02:46,101 --> 01:02:47,300
(Staring)

1672
01:02:47,301 --> 01:02:49,771
You know how you get tired over time?

1673
01:02:49,971 --> 01:02:52,040
You lose energy, become tired, and get exhausted.

1674
01:02:52,041 --> 01:02:53,871
But the photos turn out great.

1675
01:02:54,301 --> 01:02:55,940
- It's interesting.
- That's interesting.

1676
01:02:55,941 --> 01:02:57,411
- Why does that happen?
- I don't know.

1677
01:02:57,541 --> 01:02:59,241
- Was it the case for you?
- Yes.

1678
01:02:59,811 --> 01:03:01,880
Photos turned out better when I was tired and drained.

1679
01:03:01,881 --> 01:03:03,151
(Jotting down the tip from the pictorial pro Seo Jin)

1680
01:03:04,051 --> 01:03:06,080
She looks less puffy now.

1681
01:03:06,081 --> 01:03:07,481
That's why.

1682
01:03:07,781 --> 01:03:10,021
You lose the puffiness and become drawn over time.

1683
01:03:11,821 --> 01:03:14,561
In Young looks different from the morning at the house.

1684
01:03:15,791 --> 01:03:19,101
(My Star's on-and-off moments are clear.)

1685
01:03:20,331 --> 01:03:21,401
Okay.

1686
01:03:22,601 --> 01:03:25,401
(Yawning)

1687
01:03:25,541 --> 01:03:27,970
(Kwang Kyu, who looks as tired as My Star, actually...)

1688
01:03:27,971 --> 01:03:29,770
Here comes the princess!

1689
01:03:29,771 --> 01:03:32,110
Nice!

1690
01:03:32,111 --> 01:03:33,910
Five minutes before the setup!

1691
01:03:33,911 --> 01:03:35,450
Welcome!

1692
01:03:35,451 --> 01:03:37,251
Here she comes!

1693
01:03:38,221 --> 01:03:40,981
(Kwang Kyu has overdone himself today.)

1694
01:03:41,791 --> 01:03:44,121
Should I drink one of these? Gosh.

1695
01:03:44,591 --> 01:03:45,691
Oh, dear.

1696
01:03:45,891 --> 01:03:47,091
Do you want one too?

1697
01:03:48,891 --> 01:03:51,860
My gosh. This looks good.

1698
01:03:51,861 --> 01:03:53,060
The packaging is neat.

1699
01:03:53,061 --> 01:03:55,671
(A refreshing pick-me-up has appeared.)

1700
01:03:57,971 --> 01:04:01,200
(Kwang Kyu opens a packet and pours it into the ice cup.)

1701
01:04:01,201 --> 01:04:02,471
Nice colour.

1702
01:04:04,911 --> 01:04:07,981
(He even prepares a cup for Seo Jin.)

1703
01:04:08,451 --> 01:04:10,450
- What's this?
- This right here is...

1704
01:04:10,451 --> 01:04:12,520
- Yes?
- a caffeine-free drink...

1705
01:04:12,521 --> 01:04:14,951
that people drink these days.

1706
01:04:15,121 --> 01:04:16,690
It's made with black hoof mushrooms.

1707
01:04:16,691 --> 01:04:18,790
- Is that so?
- It's a healthy drink.

1708
01:04:18,791 --> 01:04:20,391
(Black hoof mushroom in one packet of drink)

1709
01:04:20,761 --> 01:04:24,961
(I'd better try it then.)

1710
01:04:26,201 --> 01:04:29,671
(Drinking nonstop)

1711
01:04:30,071 --> 01:04:31,970
Since it's caffeine-free,

1712
01:04:31,971 --> 01:04:33,670
it won't stop you from falling asleep,

1713
01:04:33,671 --> 01:04:35,111
which is nice.

1714
01:04:35,441 --> 01:04:37,941
Having one every night will help me get a good night's sleep.

1715
01:04:39,181 --> 01:04:40,681
Look at you chug it.

1716
01:04:42,451 --> 01:04:44,251
You might sleep like a baby today.

1717
01:04:45,581 --> 01:04:46,721
Routine.

1718
01:04:48,251 --> 01:04:49,651
- Let's resume.
- Okay.

1719
01:04:49,751 --> 01:04:52,591
Here.

1720
01:04:53,321 --> 01:04:54,360
What's that?

1721
01:04:54,361 --> 01:04:55,990
It's to give you a boost.

1722
01:04:55,991 --> 01:04:57,760
- It's a mushroom drink.
- Black hoof mushroom.

1723
01:04:57,761 --> 01:05:00,230
- It's a black hoof mushroom drink.
- A mushroom drink?

1724
01:05:00,231 --> 01:05:01,430
I love it.

1725
01:05:01,431 --> 01:05:03,271
- Isn't it good?
- It is.

1726
01:05:03,731 --> 01:05:05,900
But where's my straw?

1727
01:05:05,901 --> 01:05:08,611
(You're not exactly the sharpest.)

1728
01:05:08,771 --> 01:05:10,440
But where's my straw?

1729
01:05:10,441 --> 01:05:12,281
Oh, right.

1730
01:05:12,841 --> 01:05:15,781
Don't frown. What's with all the frowning?

1731
01:05:16,351 --> 01:05:18,050
- Is frowning a must?
- Yes.

1732
01:05:18,051 --> 01:05:19,280
- Here.
- I need my straw.

1733
01:05:19,281 --> 01:05:20,881
To think I'd forget a straw.

1734
01:05:22,351 --> 01:05:23,521
Isn't it okay?

1735
01:05:24,291 --> 01:05:25,560
Yes, it's nice.

1736
01:05:25,561 --> 01:05:27,791
Please send it to your parents as a Chuseok gift.

1737
01:05:27,921 --> 01:05:28,961
Great idea.

1738
01:05:29,731 --> 01:05:31,230
- It's a healthy drink.
- Exactly.

1739
01:05:31,231 --> 01:05:32,530
Absolutely.

1740
01:05:32,531 --> 01:05:34,261
(It's perfect for My Star, who is sensitive to trends.)

1741
01:05:34,461 --> 01:05:35,570
Great work.

1742
01:05:35,571 --> 01:05:37,930
Here goes the princess!

1743
01:05:37,931 --> 01:05:39,571
(Cleared the pictorial photoshoot)

1744
01:05:39,901 --> 01:05:42,340
- Great work today.
- Great work.

1745
01:05:42,341 --> 01:05:43,971
Great work.

1746
01:05:45,541 --> 01:05:47,540
- It was tough, wasn't it?
- Yes.

1747
01:05:47,541 --> 01:05:49,311
(When tired, bring on the meat.)

1748
01:05:50,981 --> 01:05:53,281
Look at me. I was thoughtlessly going to eat it.

1749
01:05:53,581 --> 01:05:55,791
- What?
- Weren't you going all out today?

1750
01:05:56,221 --> 01:05:57,990
I was going to,

1751
01:05:57,991 --> 01:05:59,761
but Waterbomb is in a few days.

1752
01:06:00,291 --> 01:06:02,030
- You can start tomorrow.
- Just eat a moderate amount.

1753
01:06:02,031 --> 01:06:04,391
Moderate amount? I'm bad at it.

1754
01:06:08,201 --> 01:06:09,201
Why are you shaking?

1755
01:06:09,202 --> 01:06:11,601
(I've worked hard today, so let's eat.)

1756
01:06:12,541 --> 01:06:15,511
Marriage... How long has it been?

1757
01:06:16,811 --> 01:06:18,981
It's been 1 year and 6 months.

1758
01:06:19,111 --> 01:06:20,241
- Since you dated him?
- Yes.

1759
01:06:20,381 --> 01:06:22,310
Did you meet your boyfriend through a blind date?

1760
01:06:22,311 --> 01:06:23,581
I did.

1761
01:06:24,381 --> 01:06:27,820
A friend of mine told me to meet him,

1762
01:06:27,821 --> 01:06:29,521
but I hated the idea of it.

1763
01:06:30,021 --> 01:06:32,060
Blind dates weren't my thing back then.

1764
01:06:32,061 --> 01:06:34,591
I loved the time I spent alone.

1765
01:06:35,261 --> 01:06:39,031
To skip the blind date...

1766
01:06:39,261 --> 01:06:42,671
I was with my sister and my friend.

1767
01:06:43,801 --> 01:06:47,571
I told the guy, "I'm fine with the blind date if you come today."

1768
01:06:47,871 --> 01:06:49,940
"If not, I'm cancelling tomorrow's date."

1769
01:06:49,941 --> 01:06:52,541
But he came.

1770
01:06:54,381 --> 01:06:58,451
The thing is, guys get scared when they see me.

1771
01:06:59,921 --> 01:07:01,821
They can hardly meet my eyes, much like Kwang Kyu.

1772
01:07:03,151 --> 01:07:04,690
No way. I look you in the eyes.

1773
01:07:04,691 --> 01:07:07,091
My boyfriend...

1774
01:07:08,121 --> 01:07:09,760
met my eyes...

1775
01:07:09,761 --> 01:07:11,730
and smiled while saying hi.

1776
01:07:11,731 --> 01:07:14,261
He has a dimple just like you, Seo Jin.

1777
01:07:16,431 --> 01:07:18,771
I like guys who look cute when they smile.

1778
01:07:19,371 --> 01:07:20,570
Guys who look cute when smiling.

1779
01:07:20,571 --> 01:07:21,571
(He won over My Star with his bright smile.)

1780
01:07:21,572 --> 01:07:22,741
You must like dimples.

1781
01:07:24,011 --> 01:07:26,981
I want a happy married life this time.

1782
01:07:28,281 --> 01:07:30,011
Did you already set a date?

1783
01:07:30,651 --> 01:07:32,721
- We did.
- You did?

1784
01:07:33,381 --> 01:07:35,951
It was simply, "Let's hold it near the end of the year."

1785
01:07:36,191 --> 01:07:37,551
You never know until the day.

1786
01:07:38,461 --> 01:07:41,091
Many couples break up while preparing for marriage.

1787
01:07:43,761 --> 01:07:45,200
You're not jealous, are you?

1788
01:07:45,201 --> 01:07:46,401
No.

1789
01:07:47,031 --> 01:07:48,900
I believe you never know until you walk down the aisle.

1790
01:07:48,901 --> 01:07:50,501
My boyfriend said the same thing.

1791
01:07:51,101 --> 01:07:54,800
Because you seemed like a pro at dating,

1792
01:07:54,801 --> 01:07:57,141
I wanted to ask for advice.

1793
01:07:57,511 --> 01:08:00,381
You want to know what men think and such.

1794
01:08:01,011 --> 01:08:03,510
Ladies kind of have a thing for him, you know?

1795
01:08:03,511 --> 01:08:04,680
- He doesn't get it.
- For Seo Jin?

1796
01:08:04,681 --> 01:08:07,551
Rumours among the celebrities have it that...

1797
01:08:07,921 --> 01:08:09,120
once he gets you, you're a goner.

1798
01:08:09,121 --> 01:08:11,321
(You're a goner!)

1799
01:08:12,191 --> 01:08:13,490
- For real?
- Yes.

1800
01:08:13,491 --> 01:08:14,960
- Once he gets you, you're a goner?
- Yes.

1801
01:08:14,961 --> 01:08:15,961
(Once I get you, you're a goner.)

1802
01:08:16,791 --> 01:08:18,400
They say you'll cry tears of blood.

1803
01:08:18,401 --> 01:08:20,031
(They say you'll cry tears of blood.)

1804
01:08:21,061 --> 01:08:23,530
It's not just regular tears, but tears of blood.

1805
01:08:23,531 --> 01:08:24,601
- What?
- Really?

1806
01:08:25,341 --> 01:08:26,941
You've got to be careful not to get dumped.

1807
01:08:28,811 --> 01:08:31,881
I was like, "Is Lee Seo Jin like that?"

1808
01:08:32,311 --> 01:08:33,341
That's how I reacted.

1809
01:08:34,011 --> 01:08:36,251
She and I had drinks together once.

1810
01:08:36,611 --> 01:08:38,181
- She cried because of him.
- Really?

1811
01:08:39,081 --> 01:08:40,951
- That lady?
- Yes.

1812
01:08:41,481 --> 01:08:43,720
I didn't know who she was crying because of.

1813
01:08:43,721 --> 01:08:45,821
- I asked what was going on.
- Right.

1814
01:08:46,161 --> 01:08:47,161
It was him.

1815
01:08:47,162 --> 01:08:48,761
(It was because of him!)

1816
01:08:49,031 --> 01:08:50,331
He's a baddie.

1817
01:08:50,661 --> 01:08:52,001
I'm the one who cries.

1818
01:08:55,531 --> 01:08:57,571
I'm guessing you treat women really well.

1819
01:08:58,671 --> 01:08:59,701
That's the problem.

1820
01:09:00,001 --> 01:09:01,940
For real? It's the problem?

1821
01:09:01,941 --> 01:09:03,270
He's only nice for three days.

1822
01:09:03,271 --> 01:09:04,771
- Three months.
- For real?

1823
01:09:05,981 --> 01:09:08,750
Three months in, I slowly want some alone time...

1824
01:09:08,751 --> 01:09:11,210
- You find it a hassle.
- and don't want to meet every day.

1825
01:09:11,211 --> 01:09:12,451
It's a burden.

1826
01:09:13,021 --> 01:09:14,880
I slowly return to myself.

1827
01:09:14,881 --> 01:09:16,720
Your personal life must be important to you.

1828
01:09:16,721 --> 01:09:17,751
- Seo Jin.
- Correct.

1829
01:09:18,051 --> 01:09:19,321
Why do you lose steam?

1830
01:09:19,791 --> 01:09:21,521
Does love last that long?

1831
01:09:22,291 --> 01:09:23,590
It should last long.

1832
01:09:23,591 --> 01:09:25,300
- But...
- I have no right to say it,

1833
01:09:25,301 --> 01:09:26,601
- since I'm divorced.
- Exactly.

1834
01:09:27,031 --> 01:09:28,401
I want us to last long.

1835
01:09:28,631 --> 01:09:30,331
I do, but it doesn't work out.

1836
01:09:30,601 --> 01:09:32,601
- Right. There are guys like that.
- Exactly.

1837
01:09:33,141 --> 01:09:34,770
I'm not to blame. Love is.

1838
01:09:34,771 --> 01:09:37,540
(I'm not to blame. Love is.)

1839
01:09:37,541 --> 01:09:38,541
(Laughing)

1840
01:09:38,781 --> 01:09:40,840
You're a real baddie.

1841
01:09:40,841 --> 01:09:41,981
(Saying lines of a baddie)

1842
01:09:42,581 --> 01:09:43,810
He's a baddie.

1843
01:09:43,811 --> 01:09:46,181
(A sinful man using love as an excuse)

1844
01:09:46,251 --> 01:09:47,881
I'm getting scared.

1845
01:09:48,221 --> 01:09:49,250
Of what?

1846
01:09:49,251 --> 01:09:51,721
- I'm the loyal type.
- Right.

1847
01:09:51,821 --> 01:09:53,360
That's how a relationship lasts long.

1848
01:09:53,361 --> 01:09:54,361
Right?

1849
01:09:54,561 --> 01:09:57,791
My first marriage didn't work out,

1850
01:09:57,961 --> 01:09:59,700
but I have a boyfriend now.

1851
01:09:59,701 --> 01:10:01,671
- What if he loses steam?
- Who?

1852
01:10:01,771 --> 01:10:03,201
My boyfriend. Or even me.

1853
01:10:04,501 --> 01:10:06,970
The relationship can last if your partner keeps it going,

1854
01:10:06,971 --> 01:10:08,000
even if you lose steam.

1855
01:10:08,001 --> 01:10:09,171
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1856
01:10:09,341 --> 01:10:12,041
But when the guy changes...

1857
01:10:12,741 --> 01:10:14,310
I don't give him a second chance.

1858
01:10:14,311 --> 01:10:16,181
That's going to cut the relationship short.

1859
01:10:16,611 --> 01:10:19,021
Why must I date someone who has no feelings for me?

1860
01:10:19,881 --> 01:10:21,451
I'm guessing you've never cried over men before.

1861
01:10:21,851 --> 01:10:22,890
- Me?
- Yes.

1862
01:10:22,891 --> 01:10:23,891
No, I cry a ton after turning around.

1863
01:10:24,791 --> 01:10:26,690
I cry a ton, but in front of the guy,

1864
01:10:26,691 --> 01:10:28,691
- "Fine. Whatever."
- I see.

1865
01:10:29,131 --> 01:10:31,061
But after I turn around...

1866
01:10:31,801 --> 01:10:34,430
(Deep down, My Star has a soft heart.)

1867
01:10:34,431 --> 01:10:35,630
Hurry up.

1868
01:10:35,631 --> 01:10:38,640
Tell me a tip on how to maintain the heart-fluttering feeling.

1869
01:10:38,641 --> 01:10:39,701
Come on.

1870
01:10:40,371 --> 01:10:41,871
I'd have married had I had one.

1871
01:10:43,871 --> 01:10:46,041
I'd have dated for long had I had one.

1872
01:10:48,311 --> 01:10:50,010
Really. Tell me.

1873
01:10:50,011 --> 01:10:52,421
I'm still a baby compared to you two.

1874
01:10:53,451 --> 01:10:54,751
What baby? You've already had the experience.

1875
01:10:56,051 --> 01:10:58,191
I have the most experience out of here.

1876
01:10:58,691 --> 01:11:00,161
We were married for six months.

1877
01:11:00,921 --> 01:11:02,560
We had separate rooms. But guess what?

1878
01:11:02,561 --> 01:11:04,061
I don't regret it. Why?

1879
01:11:04,531 --> 01:11:05,560
Because I had the experience.

1880
01:11:05,561 --> 01:11:07,301
- But you didn't.
- True.

1881
01:11:07,531 --> 01:11:09,470
What were you doing in the meantime?

1882
01:11:09,471 --> 01:11:10,571
- I agree.
- Right?

1883
01:11:11,001 --> 01:11:14,371
Don't you think it's about time for Kwang Kyu to get married?

1884
01:11:15,311 --> 01:11:18,541
The standard he has for women is very high.

1885
01:11:18,741 --> 01:11:20,210
- Is that so?
- Yes.

1886
01:11:20,211 --> 01:11:21,611
Kwang Kyu, what's your ideal type?

1887
01:11:21,951 --> 01:11:23,951
(Startled)

1888
01:11:24,751 --> 01:11:27,981
Ten years ago, she had to be 165cm tall.

1889
01:11:28,451 --> 01:11:30,591
- She had to have thin ankles.
- Okay.

1890
01:11:30,851 --> 01:11:32,821
- She had to have thick hair.
- Okay.

1891
01:11:32,961 --> 01:11:34,590
- She had to have straight hair.
- Okay.

1892
01:11:34,591 --> 01:11:37,290
- She had to have pretty hands.
- You sure were picky.

1893
01:11:37,291 --> 01:11:40,300
No. That was me ten years ago.

1894
01:11:40,301 --> 01:11:42,231
You were really picky even ten years ago.

1895
01:11:42,331 --> 01:11:44,331
- True.
- Ten years ago, you were fifty.

1896
01:11:46,001 --> 01:11:48,440
Fine. Yes, that was my ideal type.

1897
01:11:48,441 --> 01:11:49,770
- In Young...
- There's nothing wrong with it.

1898
01:11:49,771 --> 01:11:52,941
- It's okay.
- I only have one condition now.

1899
01:11:53,141 --> 01:11:54,640
- You've given up.
- Of course.

1900
01:11:54,641 --> 01:11:56,511
I just wish she had thicker hair.

1901
01:11:56,811 --> 01:11:58,580
You wish she had thicker hair?

1902
01:11:58,581 --> 01:11:59,951
(Looking for a lady who will fill up his baldness)

1903
01:12:00,251 --> 01:12:01,721
To be frank, I think you need to date...

1904
01:12:02,021 --> 01:12:03,421
for two years before marriage.

1905
01:12:05,321 --> 01:12:06,860
I'm still single because the relationships...

1906
01:12:06,861 --> 01:12:07,961
didn't last for two years.

1907
01:12:08,691 --> 01:12:10,391
- Women...
- Yes?

1908
01:12:10,891 --> 01:12:14,230
feel great happiness when they date men who really love them.

1909
01:12:14,231 --> 01:12:15,671
Of course.

1910
01:12:16,201 --> 01:12:19,371
- Keep a relationship for a while.
- Okay.

1911
01:12:19,601 --> 01:12:22,840
My mom passed away...

1912
01:12:22,841 --> 01:12:24,041
four years ago.

1913
01:12:24,771 --> 01:12:26,110
That's when I thought about...

1914
01:12:26,111 --> 01:12:28,441
how great it'd be to have a husband.

1915
01:12:30,281 --> 01:12:31,680
Two daughters...

1916
01:12:31,681 --> 01:12:33,050
- Your family has two girls?
- took care of everything.

1917
01:12:33,051 --> 01:12:34,051
So...

1918
01:12:34,681 --> 01:12:37,391
My mom suddenly passed away from a myocardial infarction.

1919
01:12:38,251 --> 01:12:42,690
My mom... When the hospital...

1920
01:12:42,691 --> 01:12:44,930
handed my mom's body to me,

1921
01:12:44,931 --> 01:12:46,330
I had no idea what to do.

1922
01:12:46,331 --> 01:12:49,270
Had I had a husband, how much would things have changed?

1923
01:12:49,271 --> 01:12:50,670
I got married after having that thought.

1924
01:12:50,671 --> 01:12:52,301
(The sudden loss made her realise the need to marry.)

1925
01:12:53,201 --> 01:12:55,371
If I got married,

1926
01:12:55,941 --> 01:12:57,371
I'd feel reassured.

1927
01:12:58,071 --> 01:12:59,680
Our family has no sons.

1928
01:12:59,681 --> 01:13:00,710
(Married to rely on someone)

1929
01:13:00,711 --> 01:13:01,880
- That's why I got married.
- You shouldn't get married...

1930
01:13:01,881 --> 01:13:03,010
for such a reason.

1931
01:13:03,011 --> 01:13:04,681
True, it was wrong of me.

1932
01:13:05,521 --> 01:13:06,980
Either way,

1933
01:13:06,981 --> 01:13:09,621
there's a need to be more cautious about the second marriage.

1934
01:13:10,591 --> 01:13:12,191
Have you had such an experience?

1935
01:13:13,291 --> 01:13:14,760
You fight, right?

1936
01:13:14,761 --> 01:13:17,730
As we've been together for over a year, we're getting into fights.

1937
01:13:17,731 --> 01:13:19,561
Here's what happened.

1938
01:13:19,801 --> 01:13:20,861
Listen, okay?

1939
01:13:21,001 --> 01:13:22,901
I like cooking for others.

1940
01:13:23,471 --> 01:13:24,671
I made us a meal...

1941
01:13:25,071 --> 01:13:26,200
and asked when he'd get home.

1942
01:13:26,201 --> 01:13:28,440
I don't bother him during work.

1943
01:13:28,441 --> 01:13:29,911
But wanting him...

1944
01:13:30,341 --> 01:13:33,840
to have a warm dinner, I only call him then...

1945
01:13:33,841 --> 01:13:35,911
to ask when he'll be back.

1946
01:13:36,381 --> 01:13:37,681
- Nice.
- But...

1947
01:13:38,751 --> 01:13:39,880
that puts a burden on him.

1948
01:13:39,881 --> 01:13:44,050
He said, "I feel like I must have dinner at the time you set."

1949
01:13:44,051 --> 01:13:45,361
"It's too stifling."

1950
01:13:46,021 --> 01:13:47,491
He's already lost steam.

1951
01:13:48,691 --> 01:13:49,861
He's already lost steam.

1952
01:13:51,901 --> 01:13:53,431
Totally.

1953
01:13:53,701 --> 01:13:55,030
He has totally lost steam.

1954
01:13:55,031 --> 01:13:56,170
For real?

1955
01:13:56,171 --> 01:13:57,830
I'm sure he wasn't like that at first.

1956
01:13:57,831 --> 01:13:58,970
- He wasn't.
- Right?

1957
01:13:58,971 --> 01:14:01,000
At first, he would've come whenever you called.

1958
01:14:01,001 --> 01:14:02,570
He still comes.

1959
01:14:02,571 --> 01:14:04,210
But he brought that up during our fight.

1960
01:14:04,211 --> 01:14:06,211
Exactly, so he's always had that in mind.

1961
01:14:08,541 --> 01:14:09,750
When you're in love,

1962
01:14:09,751 --> 01:14:10,911
you don't say it even if you feel like it.

1963
01:14:11,481 --> 01:14:13,620
- That's true.
- Right?

1964
01:14:13,621 --> 01:14:14,921
(You're actually right.)

1965
01:14:15,821 --> 01:14:16,991
What do I do?

1966
01:14:17,051 --> 01:14:18,221
(What do I do?)

1967
01:14:18,930 --> 01:14:20,830
Overcome with joint prayers or something.

1968
01:14:24,300 --> 01:14:25,370
What prayer?

1969
01:14:25,970 --> 01:14:27,569
What joint prayer?

1970
01:14:27,570 --> 01:14:28,599
(Prayers for turning over new love)

1971
01:14:28,600 --> 01:14:29,669
- Right.
- Well,

1972
01:14:29,670 --> 01:14:31,510
do an early morning prayer or something.

1973
01:14:32,270 --> 01:14:33,470
Or break up with him.

1974
01:14:35,010 --> 01:14:36,209
- Okay?
- Gosh.

1975
01:14:36,210 --> 01:14:37,409
(Morning prayers or breaking up?)

1976
01:14:37,410 --> 01:14:40,379
I'm grateful that he hasn't been married before.

1977
01:14:40,380 --> 01:14:41,750
I feel bad about it too.

1978
01:14:44,850 --> 01:14:47,389
These two aren't good at giving advice.

1979
01:14:47,390 --> 01:14:49,859
They can't date women.

1980
01:14:49,860 --> 01:14:50,860
(These singles are useless.)

1981
01:14:50,861 --> 01:14:53,130
I'm the winner for dating someone.

1982
01:14:55,130 --> 01:14:56,960
I've never taken a break.

1983
01:14:57,530 --> 01:14:59,370
I've never once taken a break from dating.

1984
01:14:59,800 --> 01:15:02,600
- I...
- Here comes the dating princess.

1985
01:15:02,870 --> 01:15:05,470
(She solved her dating problems herself.)

1986
01:15:05,670 --> 01:15:08,779
How were you in the past to say that...

1987
01:15:08,780 --> 01:15:11,010
you've turned over a new leaf?

1988
01:15:11,480 --> 01:15:12,750
There was a huge scandal.

1989
01:15:12,950 --> 01:15:14,549
- What? For cussing at your manager?
- Yes.

1990
01:15:14,550 --> 01:15:16,179
- Unconsciously, I...
- But...

1991
01:15:16,180 --> 01:15:17,880
We were close, but I still cussed at him.

1992
01:15:18,320 --> 01:15:19,619
But here's the thing.

1993
01:15:19,620 --> 01:15:21,020
They said I went on a power trip.

1994
01:15:21,490 --> 01:15:23,789
Like, I only ride first class.

1995
01:15:23,790 --> 01:15:25,530
The articles said that...

1996
01:15:25,760 --> 01:15:27,589
I didn't go on flights if it wasn't first class.

1997
01:15:27,590 --> 01:15:28,659
("Seo Cussed at Staff, Demands Schedule Change and First Class")

1998
01:15:28,660 --> 01:15:30,130
But I wasn't like that.

1999
01:15:30,200 --> 01:15:32,129
- Who said that?
- I'm not being humble,

2000
01:15:32,130 --> 01:15:33,669
but I know my place.

2001
01:15:33,670 --> 01:15:36,970
Everything turned into me going on a power trip and such.

2002
01:15:37,240 --> 01:15:39,470
But the reason I'm turning over a new leaf is...

2003
01:15:40,140 --> 01:15:42,679
Rather than denying it,

2004
01:15:42,680 --> 01:15:45,180
accepting everything...

2005
01:15:45,250 --> 01:15:48,680
and accepting the fact that I was shameless in the past...

2006
01:15:48,880 --> 01:15:50,679
is part...

2007
01:15:50,680 --> 01:15:54,449
of the process of becoming...

2008
01:15:54,450 --> 01:15:55,690
more successful.

2009
01:15:56,260 --> 01:15:58,290
With that, wouldn't I become a better person?

2010
01:15:58,860 --> 01:16:00,390
That was what crossed my mind.

2011
01:16:00,490 --> 01:16:02,130
"Looking them up and down."

2012
01:16:02,460 --> 01:16:03,559
I was in the wrong.

2013
01:16:03,560 --> 01:16:07,469
(Seo In Young admits to her past mistakes in her style.)

2014
01:16:07,470 --> 01:16:09,269
When I get tired, I lie down and watch TV.

2015
01:16:09,270 --> 01:16:12,309
(My Star frankly showed off her true self.)

2016
01:16:12,310 --> 01:16:13,610
(Breathing heavily)

2017
01:16:13,810 --> 01:16:15,909
(Do you believe in salvation?)

2018
01:16:15,910 --> 01:16:16,910
(Yes!)

2019
01:16:17,740 --> 01:16:23,920
(Turning over a new leaf and making a fresh start)

2020
01:16:24,550 --> 01:16:27,190
Here's what changed the most about me.

2021
01:16:27,650 --> 01:16:31,729
My dad tried to get me admitted to the hospital...

2022
01:16:31,730 --> 01:16:32,730
because of too much shopping.

2023
01:16:33,226 --> 01:16:35,496
He even looked up some places.

2024
01:16:35,966 --> 01:16:37,925
You must've bought a lot of shoes.

2025
01:16:37,926 --> 01:16:40,195
I had a gigantic collection.

2026
01:16:40,196 --> 01:16:41,265
You were addicted to shoes.

2027
01:16:41,266 --> 01:16:42,395
I had several hundred pairs of shoes.

2028
01:16:42,396 --> 01:16:43,905
- You were a shoe addict.
- I was.

2029
01:16:43,906 --> 01:16:46,106
Several hundred pairs of shoes?

2030
01:16:46,836 --> 01:16:47,936
Hundreds...

2031
01:16:50,446 --> 01:16:53,416
She's the first to have popularized the word "new arrival."

2032
01:16:53,646 --> 01:16:55,115
- That's right.
- Our talk earlier...

2033
01:16:55,116 --> 01:16:56,985
- Right.
- reminded me of it.

2034
01:16:56,986 --> 01:16:58,116
(Original "new arrival" Seo In Young)

2035
01:16:59,046 --> 01:17:02,856
(She showed off her absolute love for shoes.)

2036
01:17:05,756 --> 01:17:09,866
(My Star captivated the public with her trendy style.)

2037
01:17:10,226 --> 01:17:13,796
I no longer have worldly desires.

2038
01:17:14,396 --> 01:17:17,265
You still have that many shoes despite not having worldly desires?

2039
01:17:17,266 --> 01:17:20,105
Those are all cheap shoes...

2040
01:17:20,106 --> 01:17:21,305
and ones I already had.

2041
01:17:21,306 --> 01:17:22,645
I don't buy new ones now.

2042
01:17:22,646 --> 01:17:24,076
(Innocent)

2043
01:17:24,206 --> 01:17:26,546
But I do have dilemmas.

2044
01:17:26,846 --> 01:17:29,586
Can I carry this bag when I'm turning over a new leaf?

2045
01:17:30,216 --> 01:17:32,215
- I have two left.
- Right.

2046
01:17:32,216 --> 01:17:34,216
Can I wear this when I'm turning over a new leaf?

2047
01:17:34,356 --> 01:17:35,956
Can I buy this?

2048
01:17:36,156 --> 01:17:38,086
I'm turning over a new leaf.

2049
01:17:38,226 --> 01:17:39,226
That's what happens.

2050
01:17:39,227 --> 01:17:40,625
It's not turning over a new leaf, but...

2051
01:17:40,626 --> 01:17:42,355
Turning over a new leaf is reforming me.

2052
01:17:42,356 --> 01:17:43,795
Yes, turning over a new leaf...

2053
01:17:43,796 --> 01:17:45,466
- It's reshaping me.
- Reshaping you.

2054
01:17:46,036 --> 01:17:48,135
I now have a goal.

2055
01:17:48,136 --> 01:17:49,365
Turn over a new leaf.

2056
01:17:49,366 --> 01:17:51,135
In short,

2057
01:17:51,136 --> 01:17:53,505
not buying things...

2058
01:17:53,506 --> 01:17:55,435
will help me cure...

2059
01:17:55,436 --> 01:17:56,905
this disease.

2060
01:17:56,906 --> 01:17:58,046
(A self-driven change toward a new beginning)

2061
01:17:58,346 --> 01:18:01,815
But you had your struggles before turning over a new leaf.

2062
01:18:01,816 --> 01:18:02,985
- Yes.
- Your worldly desires stopped...

2063
01:18:02,986 --> 01:18:04,116
before that, right?

2064
01:18:04,486 --> 01:18:06,185
No. Back then, I still had it.

2065
01:18:06,186 --> 01:18:08,186
- Before turning over a new leaf?
- I did, but I sold everything.

2066
01:18:08,456 --> 01:18:10,125
I had to stop having worldly desires.

2067
01:18:10,126 --> 01:18:12,325
Since I wasn't active,

2068
01:18:12,326 --> 01:18:14,795
I couldn't make a living...

2069
01:18:14,796 --> 01:18:17,026
without letting go of my worldly desires...

2070
01:18:17,196 --> 01:18:18,496
- Could you not live?
- and selling things.

2071
01:18:20,136 --> 01:18:22,265
Your life had hit rock bottom.

2072
01:18:22,266 --> 01:18:23,935
It did. For real.

2073
01:18:23,936 --> 01:18:25,035
(As the gap grew longer, reality proved tough.)

2074
01:18:25,036 --> 01:18:26,106
I see.

2075
01:18:26,676 --> 01:18:29,575
What was the use of...

2076
01:18:29,576 --> 01:18:32,375
carrying designer bags and buying...

2077
01:18:32,376 --> 01:18:33,616
all the new arrivals?

2078
01:18:34,046 --> 01:18:36,045
- Aren't I right?
- Yes.

2079
01:18:36,046 --> 01:18:37,615
What was the use of a nice car?

2080
01:18:37,616 --> 01:18:38,616
(My Star found clarity through letting go.)

2081
01:18:38,617 --> 01:18:42,016
I like this comfortable life.

2082
01:18:42,586 --> 01:18:43,586
Nice.

2083
01:18:43,786 --> 01:18:44,956
That's what I think.

2084
01:18:45,456 --> 01:18:47,395
Here's what I want to do.

2085
01:18:47,396 --> 01:18:48,856
While turning over a new leaf,

2086
01:18:49,256 --> 01:18:51,925
when I sing or go on a shoot,

2087
01:18:51,926 --> 01:18:53,936
I want to be bright from start to finish.

2088
01:18:54,766 --> 01:18:55,895
It's not just us...

2089
01:18:55,896 --> 01:18:57,035
- who have it tough.
- True.

2090
01:18:57,036 --> 01:18:58,865
Let's make it less obvious.

2091
01:18:58,866 --> 01:19:01,175
- Keep a poker face.
- Like this.

2092
01:19:01,176 --> 01:19:03,475
- You can't hide your feelings.
- No.

2093
01:19:03,476 --> 01:19:05,846
- Smile, Seo Jin.
- Yes, smile.

2094
01:19:07,846 --> 01:19:11,345
Smile. He and I really get along well.

2095
01:19:11,346 --> 01:19:13,256
(We get along well.)

2096
01:19:14,316 --> 01:19:15,855
What score would you give her?

2097
01:19:15,856 --> 01:19:18,186
She doesn't have to turn over a new leaf.

2098
01:19:18,886 --> 01:19:20,756
I don't think it's bad at all.

2099
01:19:21,356 --> 01:19:23,665
She's putting in all the effort and trying hard.

2100
01:19:23,666 --> 01:19:25,525
(My Star through Seo Jin's eyes)

2101
01:19:25,526 --> 01:19:28,866
In Young is very discreet and has good manners.

2102
01:19:29,636 --> 01:19:31,635
She has her reasons. She's not thoughtless.

2103
01:19:31,636 --> 01:19:32,705
(My Star is more than meets the eye.)

2104
01:19:32,706 --> 01:19:34,336
She never crosses the line.

2105
01:19:35,976 --> 01:19:37,675
(What was the best care today?)

2106
01:19:37,676 --> 01:19:39,576
The best was...

2107
01:19:39,616 --> 01:19:43,016
when Kwang Kyu wrote things down.

2108
01:19:43,116 --> 01:19:45,185
I thought he'd stop after a few times.

2109
01:19:45,186 --> 01:19:47,586
But he kept writing until the very end.

2110
01:19:49,056 --> 01:19:51,455
As for Seo Jin, him simply being next to me...

2111
01:19:51,456 --> 01:19:53,925
He pays great attention.

2112
01:19:53,926 --> 01:19:55,795
He acts cold, but secretly cares,

2113
01:19:55,796 --> 01:19:57,626
like brushing dirt off your face.

2114
01:19:58,726 --> 01:20:00,765
Seo Jin was like a real big brother.

2115
01:20:00,766 --> 01:20:02,535
I love it when men are like that.

2116
01:20:02,536 --> 01:20:04,606
It's adorable.

2117
01:20:04,636 --> 01:20:06,905
Doesn't it make your heart flutter?

2118
01:20:06,906 --> 01:20:08,476
He had a way of dealing with women.

2119
01:20:08,706 --> 01:20:09,976
(Is that so?)

2120
01:20:12,506 --> 01:20:13,715
My Star.

2121
01:20:13,716 --> 01:20:14,875
There's dirt on you.

2122
01:20:14,876 --> 01:20:16,085
(Let me get it for you.)

2123
01:20:16,086 --> 01:20:17,246
My Star.

2124
01:20:20,086 --> 01:20:22,786
(Seo In Young is turning over a new leaf.)

2125
01:20:23,286 --> 01:20:26,856
(The production press conference of "The Scandal")

2126
01:20:26,996 --> 01:20:28,755
(Among the dazzling celebrities,)

2127
01:20:28,756 --> 01:20:31,526
(who is today's My Star?)

2128
01:20:31,896 --> 01:20:34,196
(My Star candidate 1, Nana)

2129
01:20:34,236 --> 01:20:36,606
It's been a while, Nana.

2130
01:20:36,766 --> 01:20:37,906
Do you need honey?

2131
01:20:38,706 --> 01:20:39,735
- Honey?
- I'm okay.

2132
01:20:39,736 --> 01:20:41,576
(My Star candidate 2, Son Ye Jin)

2133
01:20:42,206 --> 01:20:43,806
- A film camera.
- It's a film camera.

2134
01:20:43,846 --> 01:20:48,116
(Among the ladies making the secretaries' hearts flutter)

2135
01:20:50,486 --> 01:20:52,616
(Today's real My Star, Ji Chang Wook)

2136
01:20:52,886 --> 01:20:54,415
(Chang Wook was in last season as My Star.)

2137
01:20:54,416 --> 01:20:55,855
Was there anything...

2138
01:20:55,856 --> 01:20:57,056
that I did as I wanted?

2139
01:20:57,126 --> 01:20:58,556
(He was greatly bullied by the secretaries.)

2140
01:20:58,926 --> 01:21:01,356
(Genie will do everything as My Star wants this time.)

2141
01:21:01,896 --> 01:21:03,195
What?

2142
01:21:03,196 --> 01:21:05,395
(Fully charged with dopamine)

2143
01:21:05,396 --> 01:21:08,766
(My Star's getaway care)

2144
01:21:09,196 --> 01:21:11,136
I haven't felt this in a while.

2145
01:21:11,166 --> 01:21:13,136
You know, getting tired while hanging out.

2146
01:21:15,206 --> 01:21:17,675
People can't live by only doing things they like.

2147
01:21:17,676 --> 01:21:18,906
(Life never goes as planned.)

2148
01:21:19,176 --> 01:21:21,715
(How will the first-ever aftercare go?)

2149
01:21:21,716 --> 01:21:24,016
(My Genie Secretary)
